    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling performance tonight, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who leads the charge against Elder. His elite score is bolstered by a favorable park factor and a strong platoon advantage, making him our highest-projected asset. We are also capitalizing on high-leverage spots at the top of the order: **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) both benefit from premium leadoff roles and porous opposing starters, with **Jacob Wilson** specifically thriving against the high xERA of Rojas. **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** round out our aggressive leadoff-style approach, with **Heliot Ramos** drawing a notable +5% boost from winds blowing out, maximizing his potential in a favorable matchup against Johnson.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was excluding **Denzer Guzman**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 53.32. While his platoon edge and wind-aided park boost were enticing, his projected efficiency fell behind the reliability of **Nasim Nunez** and **Dominic Smith** in similar favorable spots. **Nasim Nunez** remains a critical component of our strategy despite an order-related penalty; his elite sprint speed gives him a unique floor in our scarcest category, SB, which outweighs the marginal projections of our bench options. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Kyle Tucker** (51.42), whose score is suppressed by the matchup against a challenging McLean; however, his pedigree keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Andy Pages** and **Jorge Polanco**, as we look to mitigate potential volatility against elite arms.",
